The [[Impractically Large Greatsword]] is a godly [[Weapon]] available in the shop for all classes. It deals the highest single-shot damage of any non-modified shop [[Weapon]] in the game, but attacks very infrequently, costing a massive chunk of stamina when it does. To unlock the true power of the [[Impractically Large Greatsword]], reach 5 {{icon/empower}}, which causes it to attack more than twice as often, therefore dealing more than twice the damage-per-second, with accordingly reduced stamina usage so that the net stamina-cost-per-second stays the same.

[[Pyromancer]]s can craft the [[Impractically Large Greatsword]] into the [[Molten Greatsword]] using four [[Flame]]s, which is an improvement across-the-board, gaining an {{icon/empower}}-gain ability and costing even less stamina when empowered.

[[Berserker]]s can trivially convert the [[Impractically Large Greatsword]] into the [[Busted Blade]] using either the [[Utility Pouch]] or [[Forging Hammer]], which is larger, becomes empowered by being in [[Battle Rage]], and scales massively off of each {{icon/empower}}.

[[Adventurer]]s can craft the [[Impractically Large Bloodthorne]] by combining an [[Impractically Large Greatsword]] with a [[Bloodthorne]] using a [[Twine]]. It is essentially a slightly larger [[Impractically Large Greatsword]] with amped-up [[Bloodthorne]] abilities.
